From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: a ScrollViewer scrolls

A ScrollViewer showed its content at its own size and never moved it, so React Native for Windows' ScrollView (OneDrive's pages) and WinUI pages could not show what was below. Its content is now measured unbounded in the directions it scrolls (HorizontalScrollBarVisibility and VerticalScrollBarVisibility, attached as on Windows), shown at minus its offsets and clipped to the viewer, with a thin bar where the view is. ChangeView, ScrollToHorizontalOffset/ScrollToVerticalOffset and the mouse wheel (48 a notch, Shift for sideways) move the view within its extent, and ViewChanged tells; the offsets, viewport, extent and scrollable sizes are reported. UIElement.AddHandler unboxes a handler only when it really is a box (an IPropertyValue that does not answer every interface).
---
